{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124373","id":4817587483,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHyaNGw","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124373","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124373.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124373.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124373","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124373/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124373/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124373/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/4150eb035a44fea75b5511f89ad290949de6f428","number":124373,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Debugger: Add opt-in dual-channel protocol v2 for Godot 4.6","user":{"login":"nowasm","id":129167415,"node_id":"U_kgDOB7LwNw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/129167415?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm","html_url":"https://github.com/nowasm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n- Add an opt-in `debugv2://` remote debugger endpoint alongside the existing Godot 4 TCP debugger.\n- Separate acknowledged step/continue/pause control from bounded output and inspection data, with lazy paged variables and disconnect recovery.\n- Add C++ unit tests for protocol envelope round-trips and malformed packets.\n\n## Motivation\nIn large GDScript projects, heavy debugger output and paused-state inspection can delay execution control. The separate control channel keeps execution commands responsive when data traffic is backpressured.\n\n## Verification\n- Built from the current `4.6` branch on Windows with `scons platform=windows target=editor tests=yes d3d12=no -j16` (D3D12 SDK is not installed on the test machine).\n- `--test --test-case=*DebugProtocolV2*`: 2 test cases and 15 assertions passed.\n- Companion VS Code adapter protocol/session tests: 9 passed.\n- Companion VS Code extension-host integration passed against this rebased binary: dual-channel pairing, variable paging, and 20 acknowledged steps.\n- `git diff --check` and local clang-format checks passed.\n\n## Compatibility and review questions\nThe existing `tcp://` debugger path is unchanged; v2 is selected only with `debugv2://`. A v2-compatible client is required. The companion VS Code implementation is proposed in [godot-vscode-plugin#1062](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-vscode-plugin/pull/1062). The Godot editor frontend is not changed by this PR.\n\nThis is a **draft** for protocol/API review and targets `4.6` to match the tested port. I can retarget the change to `master` if preferred. Related Godot 3.6 implementation: #124372.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archi